  "next_id": 41,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -30,
        -34
      ],
      "id": 40,
      "text": "A BLDC motor (4 pole pairs, 12 V, 3000 rpm without load) driven from its Hall sensors by a Blue Pill (firmware/bldc_control).\nSix-step: in each 60-degree sector one phase gets the PWM (IN, 10 kHz), one is held low and the third is open (EN low).\nThe Hall outputs are open collector: the Blue Pill's internal pull-ups on PB5-PB7 pull them up.\nWhile running, turn RV1 for the duty and drag M1 for its load; Analyzer > UART shows \"RPM <n> DUTY <percent> %\".\nPB12 to GND selects sinusoidal commutation (use a PMSM motor); PB13 or PB14 to GND sets 5 or 20 kHz. Experimental parts (E-11)."
    }
  ],
